      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended dose of amlodipine for adults is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5 to 10 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed clinician who is treating the patient. I can't confirm that this order was clinically intended.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose. If they meant 5 mg or 10 mg, they can tell me, or they can enter the order themselves.\n- If the order was sent to you as written, send it back to the prescriber or pharmacy for clarification.\n\nI can enter the order once a clinician confirms a dose within the safe range."
      }
     ],
